      "id": "1.1:1",
      "quote": "o \"MUST\"",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Section 1.1 is the document's RFC 2119 terminology section: it lists the keywords and defines them ('This word or the adjective \"REQUIRED\" means that the item is an absolute requirement of this specification.'). The keyword is the subject of the sentence rather than an obligation on a DHCP implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "1.1:2",
      "quote": "This word or the adjective \"REQUIRED\" means that the item is an absolute requirement of this specification.",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Section 1.1 is the document's RFC 2119 terminology section: it lists the keywords and defines them ('This word or the adjective \"REQUIRED\" means that the item is an absolute requirement of this specification.'). The keyword is the subject of the sentence rather than an obligation on a DHCP implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "1.1:3",
      "quote": "o \"MUST NOT\"",
      "disposition": "excluded",
      "excluded-kind": "not-a-requirement",
      "reason": "Section 1.1 is the document's RFC 2119 terminology section: it lists the keywords and defines them ('This word or the adjective \"REQUIRED\" means that the item is an absolute requirement of this specification.'). The keyword is the subject of the sentence rather than an obligation on a DHCP implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "2:1",
      "quote": "Options containing NVT ASCII data SHOULD NOT include a trailing NULL; however, the receiver of such options MUST be prepared to delete trailing nulls if they exist.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC2132-2-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:2",
      "quote": "The receiver MUST NOT require that a trailing null be included in the data.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC2132-2-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2:3",
      "quote": "Any options defined subsequent to this document MUST contain a length octet even if the length is fixed or zero.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC2132-2-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3:1",
      "quote": "If both the subnet mask and the router option are specified in a DHCP reply, the subnet mask option MUST be first.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC2132-3.3-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "3.5:1",
      "quote": "The minimum length for the router option is 4 octets, and the length MUST always be a multiple of 4.",
      "disposition": "mapped",
      "mapped-to": "RFC2132-3.5-1"
    },
    {
